<Base ogType="article" publishedTime="2026-07-24" modifiedTime="2026-07-24" heroImage="iceland-hero" title="Viking Heliskiing: What's Included in Your Week" description="Exactly what's included in a Viking Heliskiing week in Iceland — guiding, safety kit, Sigló Hotel accommodation, meals and the vertical guarantee — and what costs extra." active="" schema={[articleLd, faqLd]}>
  <section><h1>Viking Heliskiing: What's Included in Your Week</h1><p style="color:#5a6b7a;font-size:.92rem;margin:.4rem 0 1.4rem">By <a href="/about">Vegard Knudsen</a>, Founder, Heliski Travel - Updated July 2026</p>
    <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> A Viking Heliskiing week includes guiding, safety equipment, helicopter access with a vertical guarantee, accommodation at <a href="/siglo-hotel/">Sigló Hotel</a>, meals and in-programme transfers. Not included: flights, insurance, personal gear and gratuities.</p>
    <p>On this page: everything that's in the price, the vertical guarantee, accommodation and meals, guiding and safety, and what costs extra.</p>
    <h2>What's included</h2>
    <p>Every <a href="/classic-heliskiing/">Classic week</a> covers helicopter access to the terrain, IFMGA-certified guiding, all safety equipment, accommodation, meals and transfers during the programme. It is designed so that once you arrive in Siglufj&ouml;r&eth;ur, the skiing days are taken care of.</p>
    <h2>The vertical guarantee</h2>
    <p>The classic week guarantees roughly 45,000 vertical feet across the week, with more available on good-weather days. It is one reason the multi-day format exists — it protects your skiing against the odd down day.</p>
    <h2>Accommodation and meals</h2>
    <p>You stay at the design-led <a href="/siglo-hotel/">Sigló Hotel</a> on the harbour, a five-minute walk from the helipad, with meals included through the programme.</p>
    <h2>Guiding and safety</h2>
    <p>Guiding is by IFMGA-certified professionals, and safety equipment — transceiver, airbag pack, radio — is provided and briefed. Your job is to ski; theirs is to manage the mountain.</p>
    <h2>What's not included</h2>
    <p>Flights to Iceland, travel and heliski-specific insurance, personal skis and clothing, and gratuities are separate. Budget for these on top of the package.</p>
    <h2>Optional extras</h2>
    <p>Gear rental and additional nights can usually be arranged. Compare the <a href="/packages/">three packages</a> to see how inclusions scale from heli-assisted to private.</p>
    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <h3>What is included in a Viking Heliskiing package?</h3>
    <p>IFMGA-certified guiding, safety equipment (avalanche transceiver, airbag pack, radio), accommodation at Sigló Hotel, meals, in-programme transfers, and helicopter access with a weekly vertical guarantee on the classic week.</p>
    <h3>Is the helicopter time included or charged per run?</h3>
    <p>Helicopter access is part of the package. The classic week guarantees around 45,000 vertical feet, with additional runs available on good days depending on your package.</p>
    <h3>What is not included in the package?</h3>
    <p>Flights to Iceland, travel and heliski insurance, personal ski gear, and gratuities are not included. These are arranged separately.</p>
    <h3>Are meals and accommodation included?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Your stay at Sigló Hotel in Siglufjörður and meals during the programme are included, along with transfers within the programme window.</p>
